  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator 1: Integrated Roadmap operationalized by introduction of innovative and scalable solutions applied through systems integration, 2 by project proposal development. 3 donor mapping conducted.
4. Online Data Repository for the Aral Sea region developed. 5. Projects monitoring and coordination mechanism developed.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">No proposals developed in line with the Implementation of the Integrated Roadmap and no donor mapping through the prism of the Integrated Roadmap in place. No Project Monitoring and Coordination mechamism in place.
Annual Target: Project proposal on 2 projects initiated and donor mapping conducted. One Project Monitoring and Coordination Mechamism developed. Online Data Repository for the Aral Sea region developed.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of innovative and scalable solutions applied through systems integration. Annual Target System thinking capabilities nurtured, Concept Note and Integrated Roadmap for the sustainable development of the Aral Sea region is developed; 2. New Project Proposals in line with the Integrated Roadmap for the sustainable development of the Aral Sea region developed. Annual target 2</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of innovative and scalable solutions applied through systems integration. In 2021, UNDP continued supporting the initiative through AC Working Groups and systems thinking capabilities were nurtured through a series of workshops for over 60 national and international partners. A special UN resolution was adopted in May 2021, declaring the Aral Sea region as a &#x201c;zone of ecological innovations and technologies&#x201d;. To operationalize the Resolution, UNDP has supported the Government in finetuning the Concept Note and in developing the Integrated Roadmap, which, unlike traditional roadmaps, was an output of collective intelligence during workshops and was developed through systems integration, while also considering the existing institutional framework. The Integrated Roadmap is to become effective monitoring and decision-making tool for channeling financing in the region. To generate data insights/evidence to drive decisions, UNDP has commissioned Columbia University&#x2019;s The Earth Institute to do a climate risk assessment, with impact on key crop categories. Such reports will allow combining evidence with a systems lens to identify strategic intervention points and unlock financing in the region. 
 
2. Number of new project proposals. In line with the implementation of the Integrated Roadmap and to apply holistic and integrated approach, UNDP has developed two new project proposals in 2021.  
The first project is &#x201c;Conservation and Sustainable Management of Lakes, Wetlands, and Riparian Corridors as Pillars of a Resilient and Land Degradation Neutral Aral Basin Landscape Supporting Sustainable Livelihoods&#x201d;. The objective is to enhance the resilience of the ecosystems and livelihoods in Lower Amudarya and Aral Sea Basin (LADAB) through land degradation neutrality (LDN) compatible integrated land-water management. The project will ensure promotion of women, youth and vulnerable groups and equitable participation opportunities. 
The second project is &#x201c;Strengthening the resilience of local populations and promoting the green, inclusive development of the most vulnerable communities in the Aral Sea region&#x201d;. The project aims to reduce/mitigate environmental and socio-economic challenges with a view to increasing the resilience of the local population and promoting green and inclusive development.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
